LOG_FRAM_ERASE_CONFIRMED=F-RAM erase confirmed.
LOG_MULTIPLE_VALID_FILES=Multiple valid firmware files found - select one from the list above.
LOG_PROGRAMMING_APP_VERIFY_RESET=Programming application region, verifying, and resetting...
LOG_PROGRAMMING_APP_REGION=Programming application region...
LOG_RESETTING_TARGET=Resetting target...
LOG_SENDING_HMAC=Sending HMAC signature (4x 0x7F7)...
LOG_SENDING_BOOTLOADER_TRIGGER=Sending bootloader-entry trigger (0x7F0)...
LOG_SENDING_END_UPDATE=Sending end-update / verify (0x7F4)...
LOG_SENDING_FIRMWARE_DATA=Sending firmware data...
LOG_SENDING_START_UPDATE=Sending start-update (0x7F1)...
LOG_UPDATE_VERIFIED_OK=Update verified OK - board is resetting into new firmware.
LOG_VERIFYING_COPYING_MAIN_SLOT=Verifying and copying to main slot (this can take a while)...
LOG_VERIFYING_APP_REGION=Verifying application region (read-back compare)...
LOG_VERIFYING_BOOTLOADER_REGION=Verifying bootloader region (read-back compare)...
WARN_NO_CARRIER=WARNING: {interface} reports no carrier - this is what the kernel shows during a CAN bus-off condition (too many transmit errors) or a similarly dead link. If the adapter is powered and wired to a live bus, try: sudo ip link set {interface} down && sudo ip link set {interface} up type can bitrate 500000 restart-ms 100
LOG_PROBE_DETECTED_USB=Probe detected via USB - proceeding. (This doesn't yet confirm it's properly wired via SWD to the target chip - that's what the next step, the actual erase, verifies.)
LOG_BACKING_UP_FLASH=Backing up entire flash (256KB) to {path} before erasing...
LOG_BACKUP_WRITTEN=Backup written: {path} ({size} bytes)
LOG_BACKUP_NO_FILE=Backup did not produce a file - see the log above for what the read command actually reported.
LOG_PYOCD_FULLCHIP_HEADER=== pyOCD full-chip program (target={target}) ===
LOG_BOOTLOADER_NOT_BIN_SKIP=Bootloader is not a .bin - skipping read-back compare (pyOCD's own flash-time verification still applies).
LOG_APPLICATION_NOT_BIN_SKIP=Application is not a .bin - skipping read-back compare (pyOCD's own flash-time verification still applies).
LBL_COULD_NOT_PARSE_RDP=could not confidently parse - see raw output above
LOG_RDP_LEVEL_DETECTED=RDP level detected: {level}
LOG_FRAM_ERASE_NO_CONFIRM_CONTINUING=F-RAM erase sent, but got no confirmation within 2s - continuing with the flash anyway. Check the F-RAM state separately (e.g. via URTC Tester) if this matters.
LOG_MANIFEST_UNREADABLE=  manifest.json found but couldn't be read ({e}) - ignoring it.
LOG_MANIFEST_INFO=  Manifest: version={version}, build_date={build_date}
LOG_FIRMWARE_PATH=Firmware: {path}
