# --- Free tool configuration (0x1A2/0x1A3) - see EEPROM.TXT section 5 ---
TITLE_CONFIRM_FREE_TOOL_CONFIG=Confirm free tool configuration
MSG_CONFIRM_FREE_TOOL_CONFIG=Set and save the free tool configuration to:\n\n  {tool}\n\nThis only takes effect on a board whose ID jumpers read 11111 (all 5 installed) - it has no effect on any other board. Persists across power cycles until explicitly changed again. Proceed?
LOG_FREE_TOOL_SAVED_CONFIRMED=Free tool configuration saved and confirmed: {tool}
LOG_FREE_TOOL_MISMATCH=Free tool configuration set to {value}, but board reports {confirmed} - the write may not have taken. Query again to check.
LOG_FREE_TOOL_NO_CONFIRMATION=Free tool configuration: sent, but no confirmation came back (older firmware, or board not connected).
LOG_FREE_TOOL_SAVE_FAILED=Free tool configuration save failed: {e}
TITLE_FREE_TOOL_CONFIG=Free tool configuration (ID pin 11111)
HELP_FREE_TOOL_CONFIG=Only takes effect on a board whose ID jumpers read 11111 (all 5 installed) - has no effect on any other board. See EEPROM.TXT section 5 for the full mechanism.
OPT_FREE_TOOL_NONE=0 - None selected
BTN_PROGRAM=Program

